  "invariants": [
    "Delayed inquiry snapshots cannot demote formal chargebacks; won closure cannot regress, and a genuine late win may recover a lost dispute.",
    "Each dispute ID owns its closure and fees; winning one cannot thaw another active dispute on the same funding lot.",
    "Cumulative refunds never decrease and never exceed the paid amount.",
    "An identical provider event has one atomic effect; a conflicting replay fails.",
    "An existing reservation may settle against restricted funding; a new reservation cannot spend it.",
    "One loss rollup per lot prevents duplicate consumed cost across a refund and a dispute.",
    "Lot mutations, loss rollups and immutable ledger deltas commit together.",
    "Ledger delivery retries preserve amount, currency, source category and external identity.",
    "Immutable Stripe balance-transaction IDs own actual principal and fee movement; partial reinstatements remain financial corrections even if dispute status stays lost, and older snapshots cannot erase them.",
    "An actual open-to-frozen transition or additional refund refreshes the restriction frontier; all previously admitted holds remain eligible, while an already-frozen event cannot move the frontier to include newly admitted spending. Admission and restriction fences use database statement time after acquiring the account lock, not transaction-start time."
  ],
